AMD GCN:
=========
1 CU -> 4 x SIMD16 (read 16 ALU SIMD)
Each of the 4 SIMDs have their own PC
Share a common Front end / L1/LDS

A wavefront is 64 lanes and is issue in 4 cycles to a SIMD16 unit.

LDS is the Local Data Store (64K banked memory access) enables local memory atomics
GDS is used to implement Global atomics and acts as a coalescing point for Global memory accesses
In addition there are L1/L2 caches with support for register spilling

AMD Terascale 3 (VLIW4):
==========================
4-ALUs x 16 = 64 ALU per SIMD Engine

* All 64 ALUs have the same clause (VLIW bundle) 
  Technically this allows you to have ILP since 4 separate instructions packed into the same VLIW4 bundle

* For Compute you can do 4 x 16, essentially packing a PC from one wavefront in the VLIW4

* Drawback being, the slots will be unused if wavefronts have dependencies
